# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_fork_surface_honesty.py" "FORK-SURFACE HONESTY GATE: PASS" "fork-surface honesty (canonical jargon/overclaim/moat lock extended to the fork-redacted surface)" "fork-surface honesty: the no-jargon-leak gate owns the AUTHORITATIVE customer-text contract (the internal DENYLIST + OVERCLAIM_PHRASES + the no-raw-count MOAT invariants) but drove ONLY the NON-fork render path (every render_pr_check call defaulted is_fork=False). The fork-REDACTED surface — render_pr_check(is_fork=True) + the fork pause-ack overlay — is the HIGHEST-stakes customer text: a fork PR's comment lands on the BASE-repo conversation the EXTERNAL contributor can read, so a leak there is a cross-contributor leak = moat death. Yet NO gate scanned it against the canonical lists (render-interaction-honesty checks self-contradiction+never-crash; fork-pr-path/fork-neighbor-leak check the cross-PR-ref redaction — none ran the jargon/overclaim contract). HONEST-NO + WIDEN-THE-LOCK: measured all fork-redacted surfaces clean today, now LOCKED. This gate IMPORTS _scan/_scan_overclaim/DENYLIST/OVERCLAIM_PHRASES from test_no_jargon_leak (single-sourced, can never drift from the authoritative contract) and runs them over EVERY fork surface — title+summary+comment for each verdict (clear/warn/serialize/serialize_soft/unknown), the fork clear-that-still-posts cases (holder/shared-foundation/truncated), and the fork pause-ack (paused/ack/stale inputs). PLUS the MOAT cross-contributor probe: a fork PR whose engine row is FULLY populated with leak material (other PR refs PR-42/50/77/33/22, maintainer logins, base-repo SECRET/ paths+symbols, a cluster order, a hub, conflict points) must surface NONE of those base-repo identities to the external-contributor-readable comment — a breach is now a build failure. PLUS: a fork NEVER pauses (apply_pause_ack(is_fork=True) returns the notice unchanged: ack_state not_material, conclusion not action_required — no phantom gate on the base repo, no ack-label the outside contributor can add). Negative-control verified: injecting a role name + 'prevents conflicts' + a maintainer ref into the fork comment fails all three arms. PURE+OFFLINE (no DB, no network) — stateless render fns over a main_impact_surface-shaped dict; verdicts/behavior unchanged (this gate adds NO render edit, only test coverage)" "fork-surface honesty: the canonical jargon/overclaim/moat lock — which previously drove only the non-fork render — now also covers the fork-REDACTED comment (every verdict + pause-ack), proving the external-contributor-readable surface leaks no internal token, makes no overclaim, and names no base-repo PR/login/path/symbol; offline, behavior unchanged" 24
